** ~EXWM~

~EXWM~ has many advantages over other popular options like ~StumpWM~, but it also has significant drawbacks. The single-threaded
nature of Emacs makes it especially difficult to use as a stable, full blown desktop environment (a problem which is adressed in
later sections of this file), and it's hard to integrate with external tools that expect a more "traditional" window manager.

However, a fully integrated environment that ~EXWM~ promises is coming very close to "the dream" of most Emacs users (myself included),
and so far I've not run into large enough issues to completely abandon that dream.

I setup some basic keybinds, rename buffers according to window titles and prepare for ~meow~ integration.

